<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="84cd5ac8">&lt;p&gt;
    Estimate the work outlined in the Product Backlog to understand the expected total level of effort. To start, select a
    single unit of measure to be used for the estimation, the team should agree to use either ideal days or story points.
    Next, select an estimation technique to evaluate the level of effort. Some estimation techniques include Affinity
    Estimation and Planning Poker, described in more detail in the supporting guidance.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Once a unit of measure and the estimation technique have been agreed upon, proceed with estimating each item in the
    Product Backlog. Only the Development Team&amp;nbsp;can estimate the entire initial Product Backlog as they will be
    responsible for executing and delivering all of the work. Other individuals, such as the Product Owner or subject
    matter experts, can provide guidance to the Development Team during the estimation process.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    If the Development Team is not available, or not yet staffed, other individuals can be nominated to estimate. Ideally,
    in this situation,&amp;nbsp;nominate individuals with skills closely matching those expected of the Development Team.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="f2fd9d5e"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="6fa9ff2a">&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Changes to requirements captured in the initial Product Backlog are likely and may necessitate re-estimation.
        Additionally, during sprint planning the estimates will typically be reconfirmed. 
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Remember that estimates may and will change with time as more is learned. Therefore, they should only
                inform forecasting (e.g. finish date) as the team is allowed to change estimates as needed.
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        If utilizing an Agile planning tool, remember to record the original effort estimates as a baseline so they can be
        revisited later in the project.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        The Product Owner should be available during the estimation process to clarify questions raised regarding the User
        Stories, Features, and Epics being estimated.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Use the following questions to facilitate the discussion: 
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                In what sequence will each work item be completed and will this impact the estimate?
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Can completion of new or existing Backlog Items enable faster delivery of other Backlog Items?
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                What is the effort involved in delivering a given feature as opposed to another similar feature?
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        The estimate for each Backlog Item should be recorded, these can be used as a reference point for future
        estimations.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="8d804543"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="307ccbe7">To prepare an initial forecast of the total effort required to deliver the Product Backlog.</attribute>
<attribute name="alternatives" nodeId="d3a7dc4"></attribute>
</Element>
